# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# The PolicyEngine UK microdata used by this study is a PRIVATE Hugging Face
# dataset:
#
#   repo      policyengine/populace-uk-private  (repo_type="dataset")
#   file      populace_uk_2023.h5
#   revision  pinned in analysis/run_incidence.py (DATASET_REVISION)
#
# It is distributed under a licence that does not permit redistribution, so the
# microdata is never committed to this repository and no token is shipped with
# it. To regenerate household-level results you need a Hugging Face account
# that has been granted read access to that dataset by PolicyEngine, and a
# user access token for that account (https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens,
# "read" scope is sufficient).
#
# Everything that does not touch households — the scenario/price-path
# arithmetic, the full test suite, the results -> tables -> PDF chain — runs
# with no token at all. See "Reproducing this paper" in README.md.
#
# analysis/run_incidence.py reads HUGGING_FACE_TOKEN, falling back to HF_TOKEN.

HUGGING_FACE_TOKEN=hf_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
